// A2 OF gunbc.plans.fleet_machine_authority (2.2): WHICH OBSERVED BOARD EACH MACHINE IS BOUND TO.
//
// The registry (A1, gunbc.hostname_allocation fleet_machine_registry) admits every registered machine on a
// unique handle and a unique name. This admission is the other half: an injective map from an OBSERVED unit
// key to a handle, built only over machines whose identity has been grounded. Grounding is one of two
// authorities, each an arm of gunbc.machine_intake.subject UnitIdentityInputs: a physical board serial read
// from the machine (BmcObserved), or a rented provider guest's acquired provider resource id (ProviderResource,
// gunbc.fleet.provider_acquisition). A registered machine with neither is simply absent here --
// registered-but-unverified is a different fact from uniquely bound, and no placeholder stands in for the
// reading it lacks; a provider guest whose binding is not yet acquired REFUSES (subject
// UnitKeyRefusalCause#ProviderResourceIdAbsent), it is never bound by its host name.
//
// The per-machine binding is gunbc.machine_intake.subject bind_unit_key, unchanged: a second machine on an
// observed serial gets bind_unit_key's own BoardSerialDuplicatedAcrossUnits, and this module adds only which
// machine already holds it. Contradictory readings refuse with bind_unit_key's BoardSerialContradictory. A refused machine claims
// no key and the fold continues, so every machine gets its own standing rather than a whole-fleet stop.
//
// THE KEY IS KIND-QUALIFIED IN ITS ONE HOME (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority). The kind lives on
// gunbc.machine_intake.subject UnitKey itself -- BoardUnitKey, or ProviderUnitKey naming the provider --
// decided at the bind_unit_key arm that mints it, never re-derived here and never a string prefix. This fold
// joins machines on that key with subject's structured unit_key_equal, so "169308819" as a resource id and
// "169308819" as a board serial are different keys everywhere a key is compared, not just on this path. The
// authoritative identifier keeps its own home (the board reading, or provider_acquisition); the kind only names
// which authority was read and is never a second definition of the id.
//
// Consumers that ADMIT a machine read its standing through machine_unit_standing: gunbc.fleet.fleet_enrollment
// (HostBacking.unit, physical_machine_binding's fleet axis), gunbc.host.managed_host (axis 1 of the sealed
// record) and gunbc.machine_intake.arrival_converge (fleet_bound_unit_keys_except as other_units). A machine's own
// observation module still reads the key its readings bind (mtcollins1_unit_key_standing labels the ports it
// observed on that board); that is the reading this fold consumes, not a second admission.

type MachineUnitEvidence {
  machine: HostIdentity
  inputs: UnitIdentityInputs
  // The machine's out-of-band (BMC FRU) second source, on the row so a refused capture is VISIBLE to the
  // fold (gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_smbios_observation#OutOfBandArm). A provider guest has no FRU lane: it carries
  // OutOfBandNeverTaken, and its provider corroboration lives inside its UnitIdentityInputs arm, not here.
  out_of_band: OutOfBandArm
}

type MachineUnitStanding
  = MachineUnitBound { machine: HostIdentity, unit: UnitKey }
  | MachineUnitRefused { machine: HostIdentity, cause: UnitKeyRefusalCause }
  // The unit key another machine already holds, carried as the subject-declared kind-qualified
  // UnitKey -- never a bare `serial` field, so a provider resource id held by another machine is
  // reported as the provider key it is, not as a board serial (subject single_authority).
  | MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: HostIdentity, holder: HostIdentity, unit: UnitKey }
  | MachineEvidenceRepeated { machine: HostIdentity }
  // A machine whose BMC FRU capture REFUSED: the second source said "the read was refused, here is why", so the
  // machine is not bound before bind_unit_key is reached and its key is not reserved (the fold records the
  // standing with no claim). Distinct from a refused key: here no key was ever attempted.
  | MachineUnitCaptureRefused { machine: HostIdentity, standing: BmcFruCaptureStanding }

// THE ADMISSION IS ONE LINEAR FOLD (gunbc.design_argument::how_to_work: a copied accumulator or a quadratic
// fold is always fixed). The state carries what each step needs instead of rescanning the prefix: which
// machine first claimed each observed serial, each machine's readings and standing, and the standings in
// reverse, prepended and reversed once at the end (the prepend-then-reverse idiom).
// bind_unit_key stays the authority on the binding and every
// refusal: it is asked for the machine's key with no other units, and only when that key is already claimed
// is it asked again with the one colliding key, so the duplicate refusal is its own cause.
//
// A MACHINE'S EVIDENCE GIVEN TWICE IS RE-JUDGED, NOT FIRST-WINS. The second row's readings are joined to the
// first's and bind_unit_key judges all of them, so readings that disagree refuse with its own
// BoardSerialContradictory and the machine holds no actionable binding; the repetition is reported as
// MachineEvidenceRepeated either way. Readings that agree on one serial still bind it: a reading repeated is
// not a contradiction, and this fold does not invent a refusal the binding authority does not have. A serial
// a now-refused machine claimed stays claimed, so no other machine binds it while its owner is unresolved.
type MachineUnitAdmissionBuild {
  inputs_by_machine: Map<String, UnitIdentityInputs>
  standing_by_machine: Map<String, UnitKeyStanding>
  // The JUDGED standing per machine (the un-noted verdict: bound, refused, held, capture-refused). Repeated rows
  // report MachineEvidenceRepeated, but a repeated row still carries its real judgment -- including a refusal --
  // so the bound set never loses the machine and never lets a refused machine stand as bound
  // (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed).
  judged_by_machine: Map<String, MachineUnitStanding>
  // The machine's out-of-band arm as last merged, so a later row can combine with it rather than overwrite it
  // (refusal-wins). Only ever OutOfBandNeverTaken or OutOfBandVerified -- OutOfBandCaptureRefused never enters
  // the map: it is a terminal record that bypasses the binding path.
  arms_by_machine: Map<String, OutOfBandArm>
  standings_reversed: List<MachineUnitStanding>
  machines_reversed: List<HostIdentity>
  claims_reversed: List<MachineUnitBinding>
  // Value-keyed index of the claims above, so a judge consults only the one bucket a key could collide
  // with instead of rescanning the whole prefix. `unit_key_equal` still decides the hit, so the index's
  // string key is an access path only -- never the equality authority (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority).
  claim_holders: Map<String, List<MachineUnitBinding>>
}

// `bound` is what is actionable: machines whose final standing binds a unit. `claims` is every serial a
// machine has claimed, kept even when that machine is later refused -- the reservation a second machine is
// checked against. They are different facts and are kept apart.
type MachineUnitAdmission {
  standings: List<MachineUnitStanding>
  standing_by_machine: Map<String, UnitKeyStanding>
  bound: List<MachineUnitBinding>
  claims: List<MachineUnitBinding>
}

// A machine's claimed unit identity is the subject-declared, kind-qualified UnitKey -- the fold
// adds NO parallel key type (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority, ::minimize_redundancy). Machines
// are joined by structured key equality (unit_key_equal in gunbc.machine_intake.subject), so a board
// serial and a provider resource id that share a spelling never join, and the kind is never a string.
type MachineUnitBinding {
  machine: HostIdentity
  unit: UnitKey
}

// Which machine (if any) already claims this exact unit key -- by structured equality, never a
// string prefix (gunbc.design_argument::minimize_redundancy). The fold keeps an index bucketed by the
// key's `value`; this scans only that one bucket (not the whole prefix) and `unit_key_equal` is the single
// authority that decides the hit, so a board key and a provider key sharing a spelling never join. A refused
// machine's claim stays in the index, so it keeps reserving its unit until it is resolved.
fn claim_holders_in(index: Map<String, List<MachineUnitBinding>>, key: UnitKey) -> List<HostIdentity> {
  let bucket = match map_get(index, key.value) {
    Present { value: xs } => xs
    Absent => []
  }
  flat_map(bucket, c => if unit_key_equal(a: c.unit, b: key) { [c.machine] } else { [] })
}

// COMBINE THE OUT-OF-BAND ARMS A MACHINE HAS EVIDENCE FOR (refusal-wins, observation-concat). Only ever sees
// OutOfBandNeverTaken and OutOfBandVerified -- a refused arm is a terminal record that never reaches this map --
// so "no arm yet" and "arm not taken" both start from OutOfBandNeverTaken and a Verified arm contributes its
// observations exactly once, no matter how many rows a machine has.
fn merge_out_of_band_arms(prior: OutOfBandArm?, next: OutOfBandArm) -> OutOfBandArm {
  match prior {
    Absent => next
    Present { value: p } =>
      match p {
        OutOfBandNeverTaken { machine: m } => next
        OutOfBandVerified { machine: m, observations: po } =>
          match next {
            OutOfBandNeverTaken { machine: _ } => p
            OutOfBandVerified { machine: _, observations: no } => OutOfBandVerified { machine: m, observations: concat(po, no) }
            OutOfBandCaptureRefused { machine: _, standing: _ } => next
          }
        OutOfBandCaptureRefused { machine: _, standing: _ } => p
      }
  }
}

// A CONTRADICTION between a machine's own readings means its identity is CONTESTED, and more agreeing rows cannot
// out-vote a contested identity. Once a machine's judged standing is one of the contradiction refusals it is
// ABSORBING: no later row may overwrite it with a bound. This mirrors merge_out_of_band_arms, where a refused
// capture wins over any later arm (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed: "a failure arm refuses, never widens").
// Non-contradiction refusals keep the fold's last-judgment-wins rule in record_standing's judged_by_machine.
fn judged_is_absorbing_refusal(s: MachineUnitStanding) -> Bool {
  match s {
    MachineUnitRefused { machine: _, cause: c } => match c {
      BoardSerialContradictory { observations: _ } => true
      UnitIdentityKindContradictory { provider: _ } => true
      ProviderResourceContradictory { provider: _, first: _, second: _ } => true
      _ => false
    }
    _ => false
  }
}

fn merge_judged(prior: MachineUnitStanding?, next: MachineUnitStanding) -> MachineUnitStanding {
  match prior {
    Absent => next
    Present { value: p } => if judged_is_absorbing_refusal(s: p) { p } else { next }
  }
}

// ONE ROW'S STANDING. The reported standings keep their own order (reversing twice, so a repeated row reports the
// repetition at its row and not at the machine's first row), but each machine's judged standing -- bound, refused,
// held-by-another or capture-refused -- lives in judged_by_machine, and the last UnitKeyStanding seen (when the row
// attempted a key at all) in standing_by_machine. A capture-refused row attempted no key, so it carries Absent for
// u and no claim. The claim_holders index (review 94308, the linear dedup) is maintained from this same row; it is
// keyed on the key's TEXT only to find its bucket, and unit_key_equal is the authority on whether two keys collide.
fn record_standing(b: MachineUnitAdmissionBuild, e: MachineUnitEvidence, inputs: UnitIdentityInputs, arm: OutOfBandArm, judged: MachineUnitStanding, s: MachineUnitStanding, u: UnitKeyStanding?, claim: UnitKey?) -> MachineUnitAdmissionBuild {
  MachineUnitAdmissionBuild {
    inputs_by_machine: map_insert(b.inputs_by_machine, e.machine as String, inputs),
    arms_by_machine: map_insert(b.arms_by_machine, e.machine as String, merge_out_of_band_arms(prior: map_get(b.arms_by_machine, e.machine as String), next: arm)),
    judged_by_machine: map_insert(b.judged_by_machine, e.machine as String,
      merge_judged(prior: map_get(b.judged_by_machine, e.machine as String), next: judged)),
    standing_by_machine: match u {
      Present { value: v } => map_insert(b.standing_by_machine, e.machine as String, v)
      Absent => b.standing_by_machine
    },
    standings_reversed: concat([s], b.standings_reversed),
    machines_reversed: match map_get(b.inputs_by_machine, e.machine as String) {
      Present { value: _ } => b.machines_reversed
      Absent => concat([e.machine], b.machines_reversed)
    },
    claims_reversed: match claim {
      Present { value: k } => concat([MachineUnitBinding { machine: e.machine, unit: k }], b.claims_reversed)
      Absent => b.claims_reversed
    },
    claim_holders: match claim {
      Present { value: k } =>
        map_insert(b.claim_holders, k.value,
          concat([MachineUnitBinding { machine: e.machine, unit: k }],
            match map_get(b.claim_holders, k.value) {
              Present { value: prev } => prev
              Absent => []
            }))
      Absent => b.claim_holders
    },
  }
}

// The reported standing: a repeated row reports the repetition; the judged standing is in the map either way.
fn noted(repeated: Bool, s: MachineUnitStanding) -> MachineUnitStanding {
  if repeated {
    MachineEvidenceRepeated { machine: match s {
      MachineUnitBound { machine: m, unit: _ } => m
      MachineUnitRefused { machine: m, cause: _ } => m
      MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: m, holder: _, unit: _ } => m
      MachineEvidenceRepeated { machine: m } => m
      MachineUnitCaptureRefused { machine: m, standing: _ } => m
    } }
  } else {
    s
  }
}

// One machine's readings judged by bind_unit_key against the serials OTHER machines already claim.
// The refusal cause for a key already held by another machine, by that key's authority: a
// board key is a duplicated board serial, a provider key is a duplicated provider resource.
// One place decides it, so a provider resource id is never reported under a board-serial cause.
fn dup_cause_for(key: UnitKey) -> UnitKeyRefusalCause =
  match key.kind {
    BoardUnitKey => BoardSerialDuplicatedAcrossUnits { serial: key.value }
    ProviderUnitKey { provider: _ } => ProviderResourceDuplicatedAcrossUnits { resource_id: key.value }
  }

// THE OUT-OF-BAND ARM IS JUDGED BEFORE THE KEY IS ATTEMPTED (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed). A refused BMC
// FRU capture is a machine whose second source said the read was refused: it records MachineUnitCaptureRefused
// before bind_unit_key runs, so its key is never reserved for it. An absent or verified arm proceeds to judge_bound.
fn judge_machine(b: MachineUnitAdmissionBuild, e: MachineUnitEvidence, inputs: UnitIdentityInputs, arm: OutOfBandArm, repeated: Bool) -> MachineUnitAdmissionBuild {
  match arm {
    OutOfBandCaptureRefused { machine: _, standing: st } =>
      record_standing(
        b: b,
        e: e,
        inputs: inputs,
        arm: arm,
        judged: MachineUnitCaptureRefused { machine: e.machine, standing: st },
        s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitCaptureRefused { machine: e.machine, standing: st }),
        u: Absent,
        claim: Absent,
      )
    OutOfBandNeverTaken { machine: _ } => judge_bound(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, repeated: repeated)
    OutOfBandVerified { machine: _, observations: _ } => judge_bound(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, repeated: repeated)
  }
}

fn judge_bound(b: MachineUnitAdmissionBuild, e: MachineUnitEvidence, inputs: UnitIdentityInputs, arm: OutOfBandArm, repeated: Bool) -> MachineUnitAdmissionBuild {
  // The binding authority judges the JOINED readings -- in-band and BMC FRU together -- when the machine is on the
  // board authority (UnitIdentityInputs#BmcObserved); the second source contributes observations, it never replaces
  // the in-band channel. A provider guest has no out-of-band lane: its corroboration is inside its
  // UnitIdentityInputs#ProviderResource arm, so its inputs pass through untouched.
  let judged_inputs = match inputs {
    BmcObserved { bmc_endpoint: ep, board_serial_observations: obs } =>
      BmcObserved { bmc_endpoint: ep, board_serial_observations: concat(obs, out_of_band_observations(arm: arm)) }
    ProviderResource { provider: _, acquisition: _ } => inputs
  }
  match bind_unit_key(inputs: judged_inputs, other_units: []) {
    UnitKeyRefused { cause: c } =>
      record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: c }, claim: Absent)
    UnitKeyBound { key: k } =>
      match claim_holders_in(index: b.claim_holders, key: k).first() {
        Present { value: holder } =>
          if (holder as String) == (e.machine as String) {
            record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitBound { machine: e.machine, unit: k }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitBound { machine: e.machine, unit: k }), u: UnitKeyBound { key: k }, claim: Absent)
          } else {
            match bind_unit_key(inputs: judged_inputs, other_units: [k]) {
              UnitKeyRefused { cause: c } => match c {
                BoardSerialDuplicatedAcrossUnits { serial: _ } =>
                  record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: e.machine, holder: holder, unit: k }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: e.machine, holder: holder, unit: k }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: c }, claim: Absent)
                BoardSerialAbsent => record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: c }, claim: Absent)
                BoardSerialContradictory { observations: _ } => record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: c }, claim: Absent)
                // Two guests claiming one provider resource id: the same held-by-another outcome, read from the
                // provider authority. A guest with no acquired resource never reaches here (it refuses on the
                // first bind); listed so the match stays closed.
                ProviderResourceDuplicatedAcrossUnits { resource_id: _ } =>
                  record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: e.machine, holder: holder, unit: k }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: e.machine, holder: holder, unit: k }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: c }, claim: Absent)
                ProviderResourceIdAbsent { provider: _ } => record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: c }, claim: Absent)
                // bind_unit_key never mints this (the fold does, on a cross-authority repeat); listed so
                // the match stays closed. If ever reached it is a plain refusal, never a held-by-another.
                UnitIdentityKindContradictory { provider: _ } => record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: c }, claim: Absent)
                // bind_unit_key never mints this either (the fold does, on a provider×provider repeat whose
                // resource identity differs); listed so the match stays closed. A plain refusal, never held-by-another.
                ProviderResourceContradictory { provider: _, first: _, second: _ } => record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: c }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: c }, claim: Absent)
              }
              // Unreachable: the key is another machine's, so bind_unit_key refuses it as duplicated. Listed so
              // the match stays closed; binding it would let two machines hold one unit, so it refuses.
              UnitKeyBound { key: _ } =>
                record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: e.machine, holder: holder, unit: k }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: e.machine, holder: holder, unit: k }), u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: dup_cause_for(key: k) }, claim: Absent)
            }
          }
        Absent =>
          record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: inputs, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitBound { machine: e.machine, unit: k }, s: noted(repeated: repeated, s: MachineUnitBound { machine: e.machine, unit: k }), u: UnitKeyBound { key: k }, claim: Present { value: k })
      }
  }
}

// Do two provider readings of the SAME machine agree? They agree only when both are absent (still
// awaiting, refused downstream) or both are present with the same acquired resource id. Anything else
// (present vs awaiting, or two different ids) is a disagreement the fold refuses, never resolves.
fn provider_repeat_agrees(pa: ProviderResourceAcquisition?, pb: ProviderResourceAcquisition?) -> Bool {
  match pa {
    Absent => match pb {
      Absent => true
      Present { value: _ } => false
    }
    Present { value: a } => match pb {
      Present { value: b } => a.resource_id == b.resource_id
      Absent => false
    }
  }
}

fn machine_unit_step(b: MachineUnitAdmissionBuild, e: MachineUnitEvidence) -> MachineUnitAdmissionBuild {
  match map_get(b.inputs_by_machine, e.machine as String) {
    Absent => judge_machine(b: b, e: e, inputs: e.inputs, arm: e.out_of_band, repeated: false)
    Present { value: prior } =>
      let arm = merge_out_of_band_arms(prior: map_get(b.arms_by_machine, e.machine as String), next: e.out_of_band)
      // The machine's grounding authority is fixed by how it was first seen. Readings from the
      // other authority that arrive later are a contradiction between authorities, not a repeat to
      // re-judge: last-writer-wins would silently drop one authority's readings. Refuse instead
      // (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed); only same-authority repeats join or re-judge.
      match prior {
        BmcObserved { bmc_endpoint: ep, board_serial_observations: po } => match e.inputs {
          BmcObserved { bmc_endpoint: _, board_serial_observations: eo } =>
            judge_machine(b: b, e: e, inputs: BmcObserved { bmc_endpoint: ep, board_serial_observations: concat(po, eo) }, arm: arm, repeated: true)
          ProviderResource { provider: p, acquisition: _ } =>
            record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: prior, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: UnitIdentityKindContradictory { provider: p } }, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: UnitIdentityKindContradictory { provider: p } }, u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: UnitIdentityKindContradictory { provider: p } }, claim: Absent)
        }
        // A provider guest's identity is its ONE acquired resource. A repeat that carries the same
        // provider and the same acquired resource id merely agrees (re-judge; it holds its one unit).
        // A repeat whose provider or acquired resource id DIFFERS is a contest inside the provider
        // authority: last-writer-wins would bind the new id while the old claim lingered in the index,
        // silently reserving two units. Refuse it typed, carrying both readings -- the provider-side
        // twin of the board path's BoardSerialContradictory (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed).
        ProviderResource { provider: p, acquisition: pa } => match e.inputs {
          ProviderResource { provider: q, acquisition: qa } =>
            if provider_repeat_agrees(pa: pa, pb: qa) && declaration_ref_eq(a: p, b: q) {
              judge_machine(b: b, e: e, inputs: e.inputs, arm: arm, repeated: true)
            } else {
              let cause = ProviderResourceContradictory { provider: p, first: pa, second: qa }
              record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: prior, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: cause }, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: cause }, u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: cause }, claim: Absent)
            }
          BmcObserved { bmc_endpoint: _, board_serial_observations: _ } =>
            record_standing(b: b, e: e, inputs: prior, arm: arm, judged: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: UnitIdentityKindContradictory { provider: p } }, s: MachineUnitRefused { machine: e.machine, cause: UnitIdentityKindContradictory { provider: p } }, u: UnitKeyRefused { cause: UnitIdentityKindContradictory { provider: p } }, claim: Absent)
        }
      }
  }
}

// THE BOUND LIST IS READ FROM THE JUDGED MAP, one entry per machine in first-seen order, so the bound set and each
// machine's judgment can never disagree: a machine refused then bound is bound, one bound then refused (or capture-
// refused) is not. The un-noted verdict is what counts -- a repeated row's MachineEvidenceRepeated is a report, not a
// judgment, and must not decide the bound set.
fn final_binding(judged_by_machine: Map<String, MachineUnitStanding>, m: HostIdentity) -> List<MachineUnitBinding> {
  match map_get(judged_by_machine, m as String) {
    Present { value: judged } => match judged {
      MachineUnitBound { machine: _, unit: k } => [MachineUnitBinding { machine: m, unit: k }]
      MachineUnitRefused { machine: _, cause: _ } => []
      MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: _, holder: _, unit: _ } => []
      MachineEvidenceRepeated { machine: _ } => []
      MachineUnitCaptureRefused { machine: _, standing: _ } => []
    }
    Absent => []
  }
}

fn admit_machine_units(evidence: List<MachineUnitEvidence>) -> MachineUnitAdmission {
  let built = fold(
    evidence,
    init: MachineUnitAdmissionBuild { inputs_by_machine: empty_map(), standing_by_machine: empty_map(), judged_by_machine: empty_map(), arms_by_machine: empty_map(), standings_reversed: [], machines_reversed: [], claims_reversed: [], claim_holders: empty_map() },
    f: (b, e) => machine_unit_step(b: b, e: e),
  )
  let standings = reverse(built.standings_reversed)
  MachineUnitAdmission {
    standings: standings,
    standing_by_machine: built.standing_by_machine,
    bound: flat_map(reverse(built.machines_reversed), m => final_binding(judged_by_machine: built.judged_by_machine, m: m)),
    claims: reverse(built.claims_reversed),
  }
}

// THE MACHINES WHOSE BOARD SERIALS ARE OBSERVED IN TREE. Each row cites its own observation inputs; a
// machine joins when its reading lands (gunbc.plans.fleet_machine_authority P3), never by a serial typed here.
// mtcollins1's FRU and SMBIOS readings arrive from its intake lane; srv4's single reading arrives from the
// fleet lane's in-band SMBIOS producer (gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_smbios_observation), P3's first landing because
// srv4 is P9's first flip and srv1 has joined it with its own in-band reading; srv14 and srv15 join with
// their lanes' observation rows, and srv2-srv3, the Sparks
// and the H11 join when their readings land.
data fleet_machine_unit_evidence: List<MachineUnitEvidence> = concat([
  // mtcollins1 is read on the INTAKE lane (its BMC FRU rides the intake receipt, not a standing BMC read the fleet
  // lane can reach), so on this lane its out-of-band arm is the honest never-taken; its in-band reading binds alone.
  MachineUnitEvidence { machine: operator_host_mtcollins1, inputs: mtcollins1_unit_identity_inputs, out_of_band: OutOfBandNeverTaken { machine: operator_host_mtcollins1 } },
  // The row is srv4's reading's standing, so a refused reading contributes NO observation: srv4 then arrives at
  // bind_unit_key with an empty list, is refused with BoardSerialAbsent, and gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_backing's
  // resolve_host_unit reports HostUnitRefused for its row — refused, which is NOT resolved, so the cutover stops
  // rather than proceeding on a unit the producer would not stand behind. This is deliberately a different state
  // from HostUnitUnobserved, which belongs to a machine no one has read yet (srv3, the Sparks, host-6ce85c -- each carried as a record in
  // gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_smbios_observation#observation_deferrals, not as a paragraph): srv4 has been read, and
  // the read is what refused. The witness pins both states
  // (test.claim.fleet.fleet_host_smbios_observation_witness).
  MachineUnitEvidence { machine: operator_host_srv4, inputs: srv4_host_smbios_unit_identity_inputs, out_of_band: srv4_out_of_band_arm },
  // srv1, read in-band on 2026-11-11T22:28:21Z by the lane's manager (artifacts/host-observations/
  // srv1-inband-smbios-2026-11-11/ holds the transcript, the script digest and who held the keyboard). Its BMC
  // FRU arm is owed and empty, so A2 admits it on the one in-band reading, exactly as srv4 is admitted.
  MachineUnitEvidence { machine: operator_host_srv1, inputs: srv1_host_smbios_unit_identity_inputs, out_of_band: srv1_out_of_band_arm },
  // srv2, read in-band on 2026-11-12T11:16:56Z over one ssh hop from the lane's manager on srv1
  // (artifacts/host-observations/srv2-inband-smbios-2026-11-12/). It is the first machine here whose BMC FRU arm is
  // DISCHARGED rather than owed: sysfs, the type-2 decode and the BMC's own FRU all print NS1NF9000200179, so this
  // row is the first to put two observations through bind_unit_key and have them corroborate instead of standing
  // alone. Its BMC endpoint is srv2_baseboard.bmc (192.168.1.184), and the FRU serial is the one
  // verify_bmc_fru_board_serial_capture re-reads out of the cited capture.
  MachineUnitEvidence { machine: operator_host_srv2, inputs: srv2_host_smbios_unit_identity_inputs, out_of_band: srv2_out_of_band_arm },
  // The board rows end here. The Hetzner CAX41 guests the P10 flips touch (gunbc.plans.fleet_machine_authority
  // P3) are NOT spelled row by row: they are DERIVED from the one guest<->binding home in
  // gunbc.fleet.hetzner_cloud_acquisition hetzner_guest_bindings, each adapted by
  // gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_provider_observation hetzner_guest_unit_identity_inputs so the guest arrives at the very
  // fold the board serials join. A provider guest has no out-of-band FRU lane, so its arm is the honest never-taken;
  // its corroboration is the provider authority inside its ProviderResource arm. A guest whose binding is
  // ProviderResourceAwaited adapts to an Absent acquisition and is refused typed (ProviderResourceIdAbsent),
  // never bound by its host name (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed).
], map(hetzner_guest_bindings, guest => MachineUnitEvidence { machine: guest.host, inputs: hetzner_guest_unit_identity_inputs(guest: guest), out_of_band: OutOfBandNeverTaken { machine: guest.host } }))

data fleet_machine_unit_admission: MachineUnitAdmission = admit_machine_units(evidence: fleet_machine_unit_evidence)

// ONE MACHINE'S STANDING, in the shape HostBacking.unit carries: Absent when no reading exists (the
// read obligation stays on the backing row), Present otherwise -- bound, or refused with a cause. A serial
// held by another machine is bind_unit_key's duplicate refusal for this machine.
fn machine_unit_standing_in(admission: MachineUnitAdmission, machine: HostIdentity) -> UnitKeyStanding? {
  map_get(admission.standing_by_machine, machine as String)
}

fn machine_unit_standing(machine: HostIdentity) -> UnitKeyStanding? {
  machine_unit_standing_in(admission: fleet_machine_unit_admission, machine: machine)
}

// THE UNIT KEYS A SUBJECT MUST NOT BIND, for an intake step reading `machine` (gunbc.machine_intake.arrival_converge
// passes these as bind_unit_key's other_units). They are every serial another machine has CLAIMED, refused
// holders included, so a serial reserved by a machine whose evidence became contradictory still refuses a
// second machine. The subject's own claims are excluded only while its own standing binds: re-reading an
// admitted machine binds its serial again, but a subject whose standing is refused keeps its own claims among
// the other units, so its re-read refuses as held rather than regaining admission through the exclusion.
fn bound_unit_keys_except_in(admission: MachineUnitAdmission, machine: HostIdentity) -> List<UnitKey> {
  let own_binds = match map_get(admission.standing_by_machine, machine as String) {
    Present { value: u } => match u {
      UnitKeyBound { key: _ } => true
      UnitKeyRefused { cause: _ } => false
    }
    Absent => true
  }
  flat_map(admission.claims, c =>
    if own_binds && (c.machine as String) == (machine as String) {
      []
    } else {
      // Board keys only: a provider guest is not a physical board an intake subject reads.
      // The key is passed through as the subject-declared kinded UnitKey, so bind_unit_key's
      // own structured duplicate check (unit_key_equal) is the single authority on collision.
      match c.unit.kind {
        BoardUnitKey => [c.unit]
        ProviderUnitKey { provider: _ } => []
      }
    }
  )
}

fn fleet_bound_unit_keys_except(machine: HostIdentity) -> List<UnitKey> {
  bound_unit_keys_except_in(admission: fleet_machine_unit_admission, machine: machine)
}

fn machine_unit_admission_refusals(standings: List<MachineUnitStanding>) -> List<MachineUnitStanding> {
  filter(standings, s => match s {
    MachineUnitBound { machine: _, unit: _ } => false
    MachineUnitRefused { machine: _, cause: _ } => true
    MachineUnitUnitHeldByAnother { machine: _, holder: _, unit: _ } => true
    MachineEvidenceRepeated { machine: _ } => true
    // A refused out-of-band capture is a refusal too: it must count as one, or a machine whose BMC FRU
    // capture was refused would silently drop out of the refusal list.
    MachineUnitCaptureRefused { machine: _, standing: _ } => true
  })
}
